<title>UK: Novorossiisk pipelines reopen after repair - shipper.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk pipelines reopen after repair - shipper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The two crude pipeline feeding Russia's main oil export port of Novorossiisk on the Black Sea were open on Friday morning after closing for scheduled repairs during the week, a shipping inspector said.</p>
<p>Having closed on Tuesday morning, the small pipeline (500-1,000 tonnes/hour) reopened on Thursday morning, and the large pipeline (3,500 tonnes/hour) opened at about 10 am local time on Friday, the inspector said.</p>
<p>The port continued to load cargoes from storage during the maintenance, except for a weather-related port closure from Wednesday afternoon to Thursday morning, he added.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
